Z||000001||voyagerspe||10-17-2001||12:04 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-005S_3.JPG"> <P>Here's one<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-002S_2.JPG"> <P>Ive got mine in a 87 gt  great motor no complants at all. easy upgrade good power (blows away my 85 gt w/ 2.8) good mpg (about 24) ARI are good to deal with and they shipped very quickly.<P>However it is still a V6 and it doesnt hold a candle to a V8. <P>||||reg||7
Z||000002||Silver88GT||10-17-2001||12:18 AM||||I was looking into this option as well.  <P>Voyagerspe, any performance numbers?  HP? 0-60? 1.4 mile?  <P>Thanks for the info.  <P>------------------<BR>Silver88GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||voyagerspe||10-17-2001||12:41 AM||||I never took it to the track (been working on my v8 project all summer) however with a passenger with a stop watch 0-60 is about 7.5 sec. And we figure its doing about in the high 14's or low 15's in the 1/4 mile. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GTMike||10-17-2001||01:06 AM||||hey voy  do you have an auto.  cause 2.8 stick. will do 0-60 in 7.5 and the 1/4 in mid 15s.  you should be down in the upper 5s for 0- 60 and low 14s in the 1/4 if you have a race built 3.4.  stock 3.4s in fieros go to 60 in mid 6s  and 1/4 in mid to high 14s||||reg||1
Z||000005||voyagerspe||10-17-2001||01:13 AM||||yup, its an auto.  And those are Unoffical times.  The car is quick, but you wont break any speed records with it. ||||reg||7
